  "notes": "Tickchak LIVE portal — the cross-tenant listing of every show sold through tickchak.co.il (Israeli ticketing). Next.js; each category page (shows / standup / concerts / theater / childrens-shows / Lectures / parties / musical / cantorial-music / performances-for-women) and each area page (central / northern / southern / jerusalem-district / haifa-district / judea-and-samaria) embeds ALL its events as a schema.org @graph of MusicEvent / ComedyEvent / TheaterEvent / … with performer (→ artist_name), Place + Hebrew addressLocality (city_aliases), Offer price in ILS and the /shows/event/<id> page under offers.url (no top-level url, hence prefer_offer_url). ?page=N is ignored by the server, so the union of the 16 single pages is the coverage: 441 unique upcoming events on 2026-09-20 vs 163 on the homepage the Route 2 `tickchak` collector reads (it also filters to cities in our DB and links the homepage as purchase_link) — prod held 62 tickchak rows that day, all of them inside this set. Overlap with that collector: same venues + names, different source_id scheme (collector hashes name|start|venue; here @id) so both rows exist until the weekly dedup job merges them by (venue, date, name≈) — retire TickchakCollector once this recipe is live. 35 events sit in two categories: in-run dedupe by @id + id_seed=url keep one stable id. Not geo-walled: 200 to the plain Supercaly UA from the Mac and the collector fetches it from Render daily. Dry run 2026-09-20: 16 pages → 441 events, artist 85 %, price 88 %, city 99 %; 202/441 already in prod (mevalim 147, tickchak 59)."
